 "_comment": "The open ASAP7 SRAM catalogue as svGolf prices it: The-OpenROAD-Project/asap7_sram_0p0 at commit c578d6cf358145705c6dda52320cec1668ce1f0c (BSD 3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2023, The OpenROAD Project; the licence text is kept in score/sram_asap7.LICENSE). `area_um2` is the footprint of the block's 1x layout abstract in um^2 (the 512-word blocks at the corrected width 16.524 um; their abstracts say 16.0). Each block is one bank: `words` words of `width` bits, address `addr_bits` bits. Pins: clk, ADDRESS, wd, dataout, banksel, read, write. One port; at a rising clock edge with banksel = 1: write = 1 stores wd at ADDRESS (dataout unchanged); write = 0 and read = 1 puts the word at ADDRESS on dataout, which holds it until the next read; no reset. A read and a write of one block in the same cycle are forbidden.",
